Oh, it's a lot more feathered than, yeah, January 1st is the same, mostly everywhere.

213
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:17,920
Yeah.

214
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:25,040
So even within Germany, like different parts of Germany have like different first day of school.

215
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:25,840
So yeah.

216
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:33,520
I think like you don't have like this one day where like half the earth is like deciding to like get their life in order.

217
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,440
That's true, that's true.

218
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:36,640
That's interesting.

219
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:44,480
So when did, when did this start becoming in your mind like, this could be my job?

220
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,720
Like, before you went, this is my job.

221
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,240
I'm going full time with this.

222
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,960
Obviously, you were making no money at first.

223
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:55,040
And I assume with tip jars that still wasn't going to pay your rent.

224
00:16:55,200 --> 00:17:02,720
Yeah, it still wasn't much, but I got very lucky that right or like just before New Year, I added like a pro plan.

225
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:07,760
So I added like a five euro onetime purchase pro plan.

226
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,800
All existing users got grandfathered.

227
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:23,680
But that was good timing because that also meant with the increase in downloads, also my revenue like basically like ten, ten, tenfolded.

228
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:34,640
And that was really the time where I like, I like, I remember calling my dad and asking for his tax accountant because I was like, I don't know.

229
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:35,840
I don't know how this works.

230
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,240
Yeah.

231
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:39,920
It's a good problem to have.

232
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:40,320
Yeah.

233
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:44,480
But it still took some time until I felt comfortable going full time.

234
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:50,480
I I still stayed at my previous job, like, I think for another year or year and a half.

235
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:54,240
So what was the, what was the sort of thinking around the Pro Plan then?

236
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:57,680
You said it was, it was lifetime unlock originally.

237
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:58,400
Mm hmm.

238
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:04,560
Where did you draw those lines and why did you land on lifetime versus a subscription at that point?

239
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,960
I think at that point it was mainly because it was a lot easier.

240
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:22,160
Also, like, of course, like we are developers, so we like subscriptions, but as a user, you usually don't like subscriptions or you prefer lifetime plans.

241
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:36,560
So I was also coming from a place where I was like, I want to use this app to do like all the things that I did at companies which I might not agree totally like data privacy subscription paywalls stuff like that.

242
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:40,480
Like, I want to build this app to like not do that.

243
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:55,920
And a lot of that was like, of course, like not tracking users, not scamming users, but also like having a fair price, having like a fair free plan and like putting that all in a simple app.

244
00:18:56,400 --> 00:19:00,080
So I think in the beginning, I was like, like I said in the beginning, was completely free.

245
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:03,120
So I was very reluctant to like put anything behind a pay wall.

246
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:14,560
So I really only like, I think like the calendar integration and recurring tasks so that you could plan like a task that's happening every Monday.

247
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:20,160
And I think notifications that they were behind the paywall initially.

248
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,640
And then I've played around a bit with that, like notifications.

249
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:34,640
You can now have like simple notifications if you're not a pro user, but if you want to have like more, like more customized notifications, then you have to upgrade.

250
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:35,280
Okay.

251
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:39,840
How has that business model evolved over time?

252
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:43,040
Have you switched to subscriptions right or now?

253
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:43,760
Yeah.

254
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:44,320
Okay.

255
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,560
I switched to subscriptions around a year ago.

256
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:48,720
And like I said.

257
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:53,040
before, I was like very like, I didn't want to add subscriptions.

258
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:54,800
I know that feeling very well.

259
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,800
That was my 2023.

260
00:19:57,600 --> 00:20:00,800
from a one time purchase to or from paid upfront to subscription.

261
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:01,120
Right.

262
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:01,520
Yeah.

263
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:02,160
Yeah.

264
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:15,600
It's it's always it's always a big step and for me, I think the main thing was like I was getting like every month I got more downloads and at some point I was like, there aren't that many people that want this app.

265
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:16,080
Yeah.

266
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:22,720
So I felt like I will I will build this app for another two years maybe and then just everyone will have it will have the app.

267
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:24,960
Like I was looking at like the total number of downloads.

268
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:30,240
And I'm like, that's way more than the number of people that lived in the town where I grew up.

269
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:32,800
Like, how many more people can actually use this app?

270
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:42,320
And then I thought, okay, if I if I now do this, I like, I like, around the time I like started like hiring or like working together with friends on it.

271
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:47,760
So there was like some cost related to like running the app.

272
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:52,320
And I was like, okay, like if I don't do subscriptions now, then everyone will have the app.

273
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:54,800
Everyone that wants to upgrade will have upgraded.

274
00:20:55,200 --> 00:21:00,400
I don't want to like put a subscription on someone that has already bought the app at some point.

275
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:04,560
So if I don't do this now, then I won't have a chance in the future.

276
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:08,000
So that's why I like at some point and switch to subscriptions.

277
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,200
How did that go?

278
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:10,640
Was it received okay?

279
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:11,760
Was it?

280
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:16,480
Did you get that kind of traditional, you know, angry pushback on it?

281
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:17,680
How did you grandfather people?

282
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:24,800
I I was prepared to like get like bad reviews and something like that, but it was actually pretty positive.

283
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:28,160
Like I got a few emails saying like I don't agree.

284
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:32,560
Like I did a blog post like outlining why I switched to subscriptions.

285
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:35,920
And I got a few emails saying like I don't agree with that.

286
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:47,840
Like you can also just like build the app in a way where you say you get like one year of support and like then or you like get this feature set if you upgrade now.

287
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,640
And if I had new features, then you have to buy again.

288
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:54,080
But of course, that's a lot more complex.

289
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:56,240
Like I also try to keep things simple.

290
00:21:57,680 --> 00:22:00,560
But other than that, people were quite nice about it.

291
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:15,280
I grandfathered like everyone that already had bought the Pro plan kept the lifetime Pro plan, even though of course with subscriptions everything got a lot more expensive, I think by that time the pro plan was ten euros.

292
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:22,800
And when I started doing subscriptions, the one the yearly plan was then ten euros.

293
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:40,000
So the lifetime plan went up to like 25 or 30 euros, which of course is a lot more, but for the first two weeks, I kept the yearly the lifetime plan at 10 euros and like wrote a message below it on the sales page like saying like limited time offer.

294
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:46,800
So every everyone that like wanted to upgrade it was already using the app, they could still upgrade to the old condition.

295
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:48,640
So I think that's like something that's like.

296
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:54,000
very important to still like give everyone the chance to like get the old conditions.

297
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:56,080
Yeah, that's a good way to do that.

298
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,120
I've never thought of that.

299
00:22:57,680 --> 00:23:08,640
And probably to, you know, you're talking about the price increase along with this is when the app first came out, it was totally free, but it was also, like you said, pretty bare buns, like it's a it was a student project made in four months.

300
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:14,960
But I'm guessing you have been adding, I know looking at the app now, there's a lot more than what you described a minute ago.

301
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:19,520
So I'm guessing over that time, you're also adding a lot of value, you know, into the app.

302
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:20,960
Yeah, of course.

303
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:32,480
Then that's also why I like at some point increased the price to, to, to, like I, I basically doubled the price at some point because I thought like just looking at other apps, looking at competitors, that seems fair.

304
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:38,240
Like, if the value of the app increases, then the price increases.

305
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:46,240
And of course, for everyone that already had upgraded, they were just lucky or like, basically they got this for supporting the app so early.

306
00:23:46,720 --> 00:23:52,640
So I think that's something where I always try to like pick a price that's like relatively fair.

307
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:56,160
I didn't do like a lot of price experimentation or something like that.

308
00:23:56,320 --> 00:24:00,720
It's more like from a feeling like what is like a fair price that people are willing to pay.

